<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="64439" href="schedule/2015/fall/PSYC/496/64439.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2015" href="schedule/2015.xml">2015</calendarYear><term id="120158" href="schedule/2015/fall.xml">Fall 2015</term><subject id="PSYC" href="schedule/2015/fall/PSYC.xml">Psychology</subject><course id="496" href="schedule/2015/fall/PSYC/496.xml">Adv Current Topics in Psych</course></parents><sectionNumber>SD4</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Social Neuroscience</sectionTitle><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>This course is an introduction to the emerging interdisciplinary field   of Social Neuroscience. It integrates theories and methods   traditionally employed in affective and cognitive neuroscience to   address classic topics of social psychology (perception of self and   others, judgment and decision making, the role of emotion in   cognition, stereotyping and prejudice) from new and informative angles.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2015-08-24Z</startDate><endDate>2015-12-09Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LEC">Lecture</type><start>09:30 AM</start><end>10:50 AM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>29</roomNumber><buildingName>Psychology Building</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Dolcos" firstName="S">Dolcos, S</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>